  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Relation between the ratio of specific heat and degree of freedom is given by,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#947;</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mi>f</mi></mfrac><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>)</mo></math></p><p>For monoatomic molecule,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math>,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></math></p><p>&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#947;</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>5</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></math></p><p>For diatomic rigid molecule&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></math>,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn></math></p><p>&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>&#947;</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mn>5</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>7</mn><mn>5</mn></mfrac></math></p><p>For diatomic non-rigid molecule&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math>,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>7</mn></math>&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>&#947;</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mn>7</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>9</mn><mn>7</mn></mfrac></math></p><p>For&nbsp;Triatomic rigid molecule&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">D</mi></math>,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn></math>&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>&#947;</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn>